{
  "_why": "The instruments added on 2026-10-24 (owner: more companies, forex, metals). EVERY ONE WAS MEASURED FIRST through the exact Yahoo request the worker makes (scratchpad/yahoo-candidates.js): a real price, 1,500+ hourly candles, 2,500+ daily candles and under 3% FLAT bars at both - the ratio _flatRatio refuses to chart. What is NOT here was refused by that measurement or by a rule, and the reasons are below, because a list of what we left out is worth more than the list we kept.",
  "_refused": {
    "SQ, BLOCK, BMWYY, K, X": "Yahoo 404 - renamed, acquired or delisted",
    "VWAGY, MBGYY": "pink-sheet OTC: 17-22% of their hourly candles are flat, which is the illiquid-feed signature _flatRatio exists to reject",
    "XPT, XPD": "platinum and palladium futures are clean hourly but 67% and 77% of their DAILY candles are flat - a 1D chart of either would be refused by _flatRatio and fall through to nothing",
    "USDTRY, USDZAR": "a currency in structural decline is a one-way trade on a paper board - the lesson is not worth teaching",
    "EA": "Yahoo serves it fine from a laptop and our worker gets 91 hourly candles and ONE daily - caught only by verifying through our own endpoints after the deploy, which is why that step exists"
  },
